    "bio": "A Representative from Illinois; born in Chicago, Cook County, Ill., August 15, 1937; graduated from New Trier High School, Winnetka, Ill., 1955; B.A., Stanford University, Stanford, Calif., 1959; J.D., Northwestern University School of Law, Evanston, Ill., 1963; clerk to Judge Luther M. Swygert, U.S. Court of Appeals, 7th Circuit, 1963-1964; president, board of education, Hinsdale Township High School district 86, Hinsdale Township, Ill., 1983-1986; member, Illinois state house of representatives, 1993-1998; elected as a Republican to the One Hundred Sixth and to the six succeeding Congresses (January 3, 1999-January 3, 2013); unsuccessful candidate for reelection to the One Hundred Thirteenth Congress in 2012.",
